ner_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a77353f565f203d1ae9c87c15bab9252c4a754f7276a38480811a2d43e51622a","event_uuid":"9ac63084-dad0-4a16-97df-9496d72fde5b","position":{"commit_sha":"9d05542836a624f14ce902db6a42e7ff42b362d5","position":"1785005814982007001-9ac63084-dad0-4a16-97df-9496d72fde5b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"3ca86ca0-4a66-4c30-b883-1d7f630a49fb","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Dry-run evidence (recorded before the live run, per the plan)\n\nRead-only `propose_migrations('.', include_open=True)` against the real store, at\ncommit 64cefd6 (Gerrit change 971).\n\n**Sizing — 104 tickets would be migrated:**\n\n| status | count |\n|---|---|\n| closed | 91 |\n| idea | 10 |\n| open | 2 |\n| in_progress | 1 |\n\nThe 3 non-closed tickets are `119f-63e3-34b7-4f96` (in_progress, shy-fussy-hermitcrab),\n`55de-25ab-ca20-4c79` (open, harm-inlay-drift) and `be74-7832-03a8-48ac` (open,\nslimy-tuber-stoop). **None is actively claimed** — all three have `claimed_session=None`\nand no assignee — so no in-flight agent's work is disrupted. Their plan-review\nattestations will go stale (`stale-material`), which is the expected and unavoidable cost\nthe plan anticipates: the plan text genuinely changes.\n\n**A real defect the dry-run caught, before any write.** The first implementation was\nsensitive to section ORDER. Where `## Success Criteria` preceded `## Acceptance Criteria`,\nthe merge kept the SC heading, duplicated the criterion, duplicated the entire AC block,\nand was not idempotent. **97 of the 104 affected tickets are in exactly that order**, so a\nlive run would have corrupted the large majority of them. Fixed by rebuilding the rewrite\naround an order-agnostic `_splice(description, edits)` helper instead of hand-assembled\nslice arithmetic, and pinned by four new held-out cases (SC-before-AC merge, no-duplicate-\nheading across both orders, headings-on-their-own-line, idempotency for SC-first).\n\n**Post-fix invariants across all 104 proposed rewrites:**\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| `## Success Criteria` survives | 0 |\n| AC heading duplicated by migration | 0 |\n| non-idempotent | 0 |\n| fails the AC floor (`_count_ac_items < 1`) | 0 |\n| suspicious length growth (>1.6x) | 0 |\n\nThree tickets (`4702-a55c-7aeb-445a`, `8e17-8aca-998f-4f62`, `b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7`) carry\ntwo `## Acceptance Criteria` headings *both before and after* migration — pre-existing in\nthe source tickets, faithfully preserved rather than introduced.\n\nFull oracle: 22/22 green (2 happy-path + 20 held-out). Mutation-tested: no-op checkbox\nconversion, `###`-terminates-block, and never-merge each turn the relevant held-out cases\nRED. `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the script's own ruff pass clean; 179 LOC.\n\nOperator approved the FULL 104-ticket run (including the 3 non-closed tickets) rather than\na closed-only subset. Live run will follow once change 971 is LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1785005814982007001}],"created_at":1784944756854058001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1d24ffa7-cd00-4aa1-81b0-3bea02ef7ab3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5"}],"description":"## Why\n\n108 tickets in the store carry `## Success Criteria`. Their criteria are conventionally plain\n`- ` bullets, and `_count_ac_items` counts `- [ ]` items ONLY under `## Acceptance Criteria`\n(resetting at the next `##`). So those criteria are invisible to the P1 blocking floor, cannot\ncarry the `[operator-attested]` tag the completion verifier matches on checkbox text, and are\nnot individually checkable. Migrating them is the substantive half of this epic — the heading\nrename is cosmetic by comparison.\n\n## What\n\nMigrate the store tickets carrying `## Success Criteria` so their criteria live under\n`## Acceptance Criteria` as `- [ ]` checklist items.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe ticket descriptions in the `tickets` branch that match `## Success Criteria` (108 distinct\ntickets at time of writing; the migration recomputes the set rather than hard-coding it).\n\nA migration script under `scripts/` performing the rewrite via the rebar library\n(`rebar.edit_ticket`) so every change is a normal, auditable ticket event — NOT a direct\nrewrite of the git-backed store.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: closed tickets' historical accuracy is not preserved by rewriting; see Approach\nfor why closed tickets are migrated too and what that costs.\n\n## Approach\n\nFor each matching ticket: locate the `## Success Criteria` block (bounded by the next `## `\nheading), convert its `- ` bullets to `- [ ]` items, and merge them into the ticket's existing\n`## Acceptance Criteria` block, appending if one exists and creating it if not. Tickets already\ncarrying both headings merge; the SC heading is then removed.\n\nEditing a ticket's description changes its MATERIAL FINGERPRINT, which invalidates any\nplan-review attestation as `stale-material`. That is correct and unavoidable — the plan text\ngenuinely changed — but it means the migration must not be run blindly across claimed work.\nThe script therefore processes CLOSED tickets by default and requires an explicit flag to touch\nopen/in_progress ones, so no in-flight claim is silently invalidated. The count of skipped\nin-flight tickets is reported so the remainder can be migrated deliberately.\n\nRun as a dry-run first, with the diff recorded on this ticket before the live run.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit tests for the block-rewriting function over fixtures: SC-only, both-headings, SC with\n  mixed `- ` and `- [ ]` items, SC as the LAST section (no following `##`), and a ticket with\n  no SC block (must be a no-op).\n- Dry-run over the real store, with the resulting diff attached as a ticket comment.\n- Post-migration assertion that `_count_ac_items` returns >=1 for every migrated ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A script under `scripts/` performs the migration through `rebar.edit_ticket`, with\n      `--dry-run` as the default mode and a required explicit flag to modify non-closed tickets.\n- [ ] Unit tests cover all five block-shape cases listed under Testing, including the no-op case.\n- [ ] After the live run, `git grep -l \"## Success Criteria\" tickets` matches no ticket\n      description outside the skipped in-flight set.\n- [ ] Every migrated ticket returns `_count_ac_items >= 1`, verified by a script pass over the\n      migrated set.\n- [ ] The dry-run diff and the list of skipped in-flight tickets are recorded as comments on\n      this ticket.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/migrate_success_criteria.py","reason":"New migration script driving rebar.edit_ticket"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_migrate_success_criteria.py","reason":"Block-rewriting unit tests over five fixture shapes"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5"],["parent","1386-5e7c-391d-4a74"]],"parent_id":"1386-5e7c-391d-4a74","parent_status_uuid":"48ba7936-6600-48c5-9d56-3bf54effa12c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["vocabulary","plan-review"],"ticket_id":"0a8c-f7b1-6828-468c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate store tickets from Success Criteria bullets to Acceptance Criteria checkboxes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["81fd3e99-21a3-4e05-9352-20ce757e7ebb","1d24ffa7-cd00-4aa1-81b0-3bea02ef7ab3","a67243eb-9bcc-4b9d-beab-672f2cd64b71","c01bd2ad-8aa4-40e7-af98-f73a01bfce79","26aaa2e5-168b-481e-ad17-b387c399c332","48ba7936-6600-48c5-9d56-3bf54effa12c","d95ece5f-1e3e-427c-93e1-fb221bb42926","dbd13bbe-fce1-4be2-a1c9-78ecde23dced","9ac63084-dad0-4a16-97df-9496d72fde5b"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785005814982007002,"uuid":"3ea682fb-b176-47c2-8e80-3f35a9cd4f1f"}